 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Lines 152-155 declare `size_def`/`impactParameter_def` with no attribute; `size` (line 147) and `impactParameter` (line 150) are plain `def`s in a `public section` without `@[expose]`, so simp has no equation lemma for them. Roadmap SmallXAndSaturation/README.md:329 requires the derived coordinates to come \"with ... the simp lemmas\", and Convention 4 (README.md:119-121) keeps the two endpoints as the data that downstream statements are written in, so `Dipole.mk x y` is the entry point that needs them.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/SmallX/Dipole/Coordinates.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] lemma size_mk (x y : EuclideanSpace \u211d (Fin 2)) : (Dipole.mk x y).size = x - y := (rfl)` and `@[simp] lemma impactParameter_mk (x y : EuclideanSpace \u211d (Fin 2)) : (Dipole.mk x y).impactParameter = midpoint \u211d x y := (rfl)`, next to `size_def`/`impactParameter_def`.",
   "issue": "`size_def` (line 152) and `impactParameter_def` (line 154) are the only route from a dipole given by its constructor to its derived coordinates, and neither carries `@[simp]` (correctly, since as stated they would unfold everywhere). There is no `@[simp] size_mk` / `impactParameter_mk`, so `simp` cannot prove `(\u27e8x, y\u27e9 : Dipole).size = x - y` or `(\u27e8x, y\u27e9 : Dipole).impactParameter = midpoint \u211d x y` without `simp [size_def]`. This is asymmetric with `ofSizeImpactParameter`, which gets `quark_`/`antiquark_`/`size_`/`impactParameter_ofSizeImpactParameter` all `@[simp]` (lines 215-231), and the roadmap names simp lemmas on the derived coordinates as part of the \u00a70.1 deliverable.",
   "line": 152
  }
 ],
